{"id": "EUVD-2026-101221", "enisaUuid": "8b5c8ff2-52f0-33a0-aca8-ad706a0e94ba", "description": "BottleCRM through 1.14.5 contains a server-side template injection vulnerability in the send_email Celery task, which compiles the user-supplied AccountEmail message_body with django.template.Template(). Authenticated organization members can submit template tags through POST /api/accounts/<id>/create_mail/ to disclose the rendering context and loaded Python modules, or block the shared Celery worker with nested loops.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T11:38:59", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/issues/826", "https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/blob/v1.14.5/backend/accounts/tasks.py#L45", "https://github.com/aaronamran/CVE-Disclosures/tree/main/CVE-2026/CVE-2026-110593", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bottlecrm-through-1.14.5-server-side-template-injection-via-account-email-create-mail"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110593", "GHSA-j2m5-qh4m-hfjr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23449e54-61b4-30a8-a59e-16511e07a51d", "product": {"name": "BottleCRM", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.14.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "379d5151-a249-3cb7-acfa-95ecffb7e6a8", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}], "isExploited": false}